I'm not completely familiar with Mingw or Cygwin, but here are my 2 eurocents.
You NEED make. make is a program that tells gcc how to compile each file, how
to combine them and in which order they should be compiled.

Just as an example: I'm building something else on this machine now. Currently,
it's doing this:

> i686-pc-linux-gnu-gcc -DHAVE_CONFIG_H -I. -I. -I..
> -DGNOMELOCALEDIR=\""/usr/share/locale"\" -I.. -DBONOBO_UI_INTERNAL
> -DBONOBO_UIDIR=\""/usr/share/gnome/ui/"\" -DBONOBO_TOPSRCDIR=\"".."\"
> -DG_LOG_DOMAIN=\"Bonobo\" -DVERSION=\"2.14.0\" -Wall -Wmissing-prototypes
> -DORBIT2=1 -pthread -I/usr/include/libgnomecanvas-2.0
> -I/usr/include/libart-2.0 -I/usr/include/pango-1.0 -I/usr/include/freetype2
> -I/usr/include/gtk-2.0 -I/usr/include/glib-2.0 -I/usr/lib/glib-2.0/include
> -I/usr/lib/gtk-2.0/include -I/usr/include/atk-1.0 -I/usr/include/cairo
> -I/usr/include/libbonobo-2.0 -I/usr/include/orbit-2.0
> -I/usr/include/bonobo-activation-2.0 -I/usr/include/libgnome-2.0
> -I/usr/include/gconf/2 -I/usr/include/gnome-vfs-2.0
> -I/usr/lib/gnome-vfs-2.0/include -I/usr/include/libxml2      -O2
> -march=pentium3 -mcpu=pentium3 -pipe -mcpu=i686 -fomit-frame-pointer -c `test
> -f 'test-toolbar.c' || echo './'`test-toolbar.c

and that's only 1 file. The nethack source contains 107 of these files. make is
made to save you from that typing horror.

I guess you need some package from one of either "distribution". I see mingw has
a make package on its frontpage. 

You need to edit the Makefile a bit. Refer to the Install.nt file in the
sys/winnt directory of you source copy.

